# Form in a drawer with a live page

Reference implementation: `get_doc("docs:/guides/forms/forms-in-overlays/")` (example `docs:/examples/drawer-form/`). Read it first; the steps below are its shape.

1. Define the form once, shared by page and action (any Standard Schema library):

```ts
// src/forms/customer.ts
import { defineForm } from "@rivetjs/forms";
import { z } from "zod";
export const customerForm = defineForm({ name: "customer", schema: z.object({ name: z.string().min(1), email: z.string().email() }) });
```

2. Make the page live and add the action:

```tsx
import type { LivePageProps } from "@rivetjs/router";
import { actionResult } from "@rivetjs/router/client";
import { action, invalid } from "@rivetjs/forms/server";

export const live = true; // data is an accessor, refreshed in place after a submit: signals (open drawer, input, focus) survive
export const serverLoad = ({ url }: { url: URL }) => ({ customers: [...customers], creating: url.searchParams.has("new") });
export const serverActions = {
  customer: action(customerForm, (value) => {
    if (customers.some((c) => c.email === value.email)) return invalid({ email: "Already a customer" });
    customers.push({ id: customers.length + 1, ...value });
  }),
};
export default function Customers({ data }: LivePageProps<typeof serverLoad>) {
  /* … */
}
```

3. In the component: `const result = actionResult("customer")`, `const open = signal(data().creating || (result?.status ?? 0) >= 400)` (no-JS entry: `<a href="?new" onClick={(e) => { e.preventDefault(); open.set(true); }}>`), `const form = createForm(customerForm, { result })`. Render the list from `data()` with `<For each={data().customers} by={(c) => c.id}>`; never copy `data()` into a signal.
4. The overlay: `@rivetjs/ui` (`Drawer` / `Modal`, `isOpen={open}`) or cdk `ModalOverlay isDismissable isOpen={open}` + `Modal` + `Dialog` (div overlay layer, two-way `isOpen`). The form inside:

```tsx
<form id={formId(form)} method="post" action="?/customer" onSubmit={async (event) => (await onSubmit(customerForm, form, event)) && open.set(false)}>
  <label for={fieldId(form, "email")}>Email</label>
  <input
    id={fieldId(form, "email")}
    name="email"
    value={defaultValue(form, "email")}
    aria-invalid={isInvalid(form, "email")}
    aria-describedby={describedBy(form, "email")}
  />
  <FieldError of={form} name="email" />
  <button aria-disabled={submitting(form) ? "true" : undefined}>Save</button>
</form>
```

`onSubmit` resolves true once the server accepted the form and the page data is fresh: close the drawer then. Errors stay in the open drawer. Imports: `createForm, defaultValue, describedBy, fieldId, formId, isInvalid, onSubmit, submitting` from `@rivetjs/forms`, `FieldError` from `@rivetjs/forms/components`.

5. A layout `serverLoad` re-runs too (counts in headers update).
6. Check: `check_code` on the page, `npm run check`, then try it with JavaScript disabled (plain POST, 400 re-render with the drawer open).
